i.github.com/users/buckbaskin","html_url":"https://github.com/buckbaskin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/buckbaskin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/buckbaskin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/buckbaskin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/buckbaskin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/buckbaskin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/buckbaskin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/buckbaskin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/buckbaskin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/buckbaskin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-09-21T23:05:21Z","updated_at":"2016-09-21T23:05:21Z","body":"It looks like the type checking code for bytes is just to use the string version (see [checkexpr.py](https://github.com/python/mypy/blob/345a4571cff9fd5942bc5c0a95044f792cf8bd19/mypy/checkexpr.py#L968-L969)). The lines effectively check to see if it either matches `StrExpr` or `BytesExpr` and casts to `StrExpr` if it matches either one. This leads to the bug, where the BytesExpr is supposed to stay a BytesExpr.\n\nWould the correct way to fix this be to create a new checker for Bytes? Or possibly to add a method to what is now StringFormatterChecker that checks bytes instead?\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/comments/248769109/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"buckbaskin","id":3441311,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0NDEzMTE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3441311?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/buckbaskin","html_url":"https://github.com/buckbaskin","followers_url":